  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The vernier scale used for measurement has a positive zero error of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;If while taking a measurement it was noted that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math> on the vernier scale lies between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>.&nbsp;Vernier coincidence is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the correct value of measurement is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>(least count<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>)</p>"
